DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rruusseerrss command produces output similar to who(1), but for the list of
     _h_o_s_ts or all machines on the local network.  For each _h_o_s_t responding to
     the rruusseerrss query, the hostname with the names of the users currently
     logged on is printed on each line.  The rruusseerrss command will wait for one
     minute to catch late responders.

     The following options are available:

     --aa      Print all machines responding even if no one is currently logged
             in.

     --ll      Print a long format listing.  This includes the user name, host
             name, tty that the user is logged in to, the date and time the
             user logged in, the amount of time since the user typed on the
             keyboard, and the remote host they logged in from (if applica‐
             ble).

